## Environment Setup

*Instructions on how to set up the isolated computational environment to run the analysis scripts. Choose the package manager that fits your workflow.*

```bash
# Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/username/{{project_name}}.git
cd {{project_name}}
```

### Option 1: uv

```bash
# uv sync automatically creates the .venv and installs dependencies from pyproject.toml
uv sync
source .venv/bin/activate  # On Windows use `.venv\Scripts\activate`, or run via WSL2 terminal
```

### Option 2: Standard pip (venv)

```bash
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate  # On Windows use `.venv\Scripts\activate`, or run via WSL2 terminal
pip install .              # Installs dependencies listed in pyproject.toml
```

### Option 3: Poetry

```bash
poetry install
poetry shell
```

## Usage

*Explain how to run the project.*

{% if include_notebooks -%}
Start with `notebooks/data_processing_notebook.ipynb` to clean and validate the data{% if include_reports %}, logging changes in `reports/cleaning_log.md` as you go{% endif %}.
Move to `notebooks/data_analysis_notebook.ipynb` for exploratory analysis{% if include_reports %}, then write up findings in `reports/REPORT.md`{% endif %}.
{% endif -%}
{% if include_module -%}
Shared helper functions used across notebooks live in `src/{{module_name}}/` — it installs in editable mode via `uv sync`, so it's importable from notebooks without extra path setup.
